    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! The bug is now fixed. Here's what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Problem:** The `frai gate init --ci` command wasn't creating the GitHub Actions workflow file `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`, even though running `frai-gate init --ci` directly worked.\n\n**Root Cause:** In the frai CLI's gate command handler, commander's argument parsing wasn't properly capturing the `--ci` flag when passing arguments to the frai-gate CLI via `spawnSync()`.\n\n**Solution:** Modified `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to extract arguments directly from `process.argv` instead of relying on commander's parsed `args` parameter. This ensures all flags and options (including `--ci`) are properly forwarded to the frai-gate subprocess.\n\n**Changes Made:**\n- Updated the gate command action to find the 'gate' index in `process.argv` \n- Extracted all arguments after 'gate' from the raw argv\n- Passed these arguments directly to the frai-gate CLI\n\n**Verification:** \u2705 Tested the fix in a clean directory - both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` are now created correctly with the `--ci` flag.",
